      "content": "That's a good start, it sounds very professional. But I'm worried the council might push back if we just talk about \"buildings\" and \"businesses.\" They'll want to know *why* it feels so disjointed and why it hasn't attracted people yet. Can we be a bit more specific about the social landscape? I want to hint at the fact that the current demographic and the general atmosphere of the streets/neighborhood are what's primarily holding back the \"upmarket\" crowd without being too blunt about it. Give me some descriptors for the current community vibe that would justify needing a new kind of resident.",
